// IAccount.fol — package source file
// Spec: language-ref.md > Interfaces, Interface vs Signature
//
// An interface is a BEHAVIOURAL contract tied to class dispatch and
// polymorphism. It is implemented by classes via `implements=[]`, supports
// virtual and dynamic dispatch, and each implementing class may create any
// number of independent objects with their own state.
//
// An interface contains method specifications only — no values, no type
// components, no nested or target-local declarations. Each specification is a
// forward form and ends with a semicolon.

_ co.lang.interface = {
    deposit(amount co.lang.int)->(co.lang.int);
    statement()->(co.lang.string);
}
